1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:50,728
I said it, without even thinking.

2
00:01:52,228 --> 00:01:53,988
I want to go somewhere.

3
00:01:55,408 --> 00:01:56,428
Go where?

4
00:01:57,708 --> 00:01:59,528
Is there some place you have in mind?

5
00:01:59,768 --> 00:02:00,148
Where?

6
00:02:00,148 --> 00:02:04,488
What's that? It looks good.

7
00:02:04,608 --> 00:02:06,788
Can I have a taste just a little, please?

8
00:02:06,848 --> 00:02:08,088
I know where I'd like to go.

9
00:02:10,908 --> 00:02:12,568
I want to go to Milky Land.

10
00:02:13,448 --> 00:02:14,668
Enoshima looks fun.

11
00:02:15,428 --> 00:02:17,568
And Chinatown, don't you think?

12
00:02:17,868 --> 00:02:21,728
With meat dumplings, shrimp and chili sauce, and almond jelly.

13
00:02:22,068 --> 00:02:24,428
So good! I want to find potatoes.

14
00:02:24,868 --> 00:02:27,748
And then we can go to Soisa's factory.

15
00:02:28,088 --> 00:02:29,868
You want to go there again, Momo?

16
00:02:30,348 --> 00:02:32,668
Didn't you already visit the factory on a field trip?

17
00:02:32,928 --> 00:02:35,528
They want to know where you want to go, not where you've been.

18
00:02:35,728 --> 00:02:38,248
She did have a lot of fun digging up those potatoes.

19
00:02:38,808 --> 00:02:40,408
She always talks about it.

20
00:02:41,168 --> 00:02:42,788
Is there anywhere you'd like to go?

21
00:02:42,788 --> 00:02:46,048
Let's see.

22
00:02:46,048 --> 00:02:52,128
I guess I'd want to go to a beautiful beach where I can just relax for a while.

23
00:02:52,708 --> 00:02:57,228
I'd take a nap, get a makeover, and maybe an aromatherapy massage.

24
00:02:57,228 --> 00:03:03,308
But I'd be happy just to have a vacation from cooking.

25
00:03:03,728 --> 00:03:04,628
That'd be nice.

26
00:03:05,168 --> 00:03:06,228
But anyway...

27
00:03:06,768 --> 00:03:08,728
Thank you for always taking care of us.

28
00:03:08,728 --> 00:03:12,788
If you ask me, let me think.

29
00:03:14,108 --> 00:03:16,208
I suppose the Issei Grand Shrine.

30
00:03:16,428 --> 00:03:18,368
Your grandmother always wanted to go there.

31
00:03:18,368 --> 00:03:23,108
So how about you, kid?

32
00:03:23,548 --> 00:03:25,548
Where do you want to go since you brought it up?

33
00:03:25,548 --> 00:03:33,508
I didn't realize until he asked me.

34
00:03:34,988 --> 00:03:37,248
There wasn't anywhere I really wanted to go.

35
00:03:41,748 --> 00:03:45,248
When I thought about it, I didn't want to go anywhere specific.

36
00:03:46,028 --> 00:03:47,848
I just wanted to be somewhere else.

37
00:03:48,428 --> 00:03:49,208
Anywhere else.

38
00:03:57,168 --> 00:03:58,168
So, Kiriyama.

39
00:03:58,168 --> 00:04:01,748
I hear that you're not participating in the study camp this year.

40
00:04:03,388 --> 00:04:06,308
With your rank deciding competition, I guess I can't blame you.

41
00:04:07,068 --> 00:04:09,988
You are a pro now, and work comes first.

42
00:04:10,648 --> 00:04:12,248
Missing a match is totally forbidden.

43
00:04:12,848 --> 00:04:15,608
The only exception is for funerals of immediate family.

44
00:04:15,608 --> 00:04:19,748
Well, it's too bad you'll have to miss it.

45
00:04:20,148 --> 00:04:24,488
As far as school events go, study camps are usually a pretty major part of a student's life.

46
00:04:26,428 --> 00:04:26,908
Oh.

47
00:04:29,248 --> 00:04:31,088
It's true I was a little disappointed.

48
00:04:32,428 --> 00:04:34,388
Not disappointed that I couldn't go,

49
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:36,428
but disappointed in myself

50
00:04:36,428 --> 00:04:39,568
for being secretly relieved that I got out of going.

51
00:04:40,188 --> 00:04:41,628
Having said that,

52
00:04:41,628 --> 00:04:44,388
you don't have to make it so obvious

53
00:04:44,388 --> 00:04:45,928
that you're relieved about not going.

54
00:04:46,168 --> 00:04:47,648
Crap, he saw right through me.

55
00:04:49,128 --> 00:04:51,068
Oh no, is it really that obvious?

56
00:04:51,788 --> 00:04:53,588
Look, I get where you're coming from.

57
00:04:53,828 --> 00:04:54,988
You don't have any friends,

58
00:04:55,328 --> 00:04:57,448
you'd be thrown in with a group of random guys

59
00:04:57,448 --> 00:04:58,648
you don't really even know,

60
00:04:58,708 --> 00:04:59,748
and that could be rough.

61
00:04:59,968 --> 00:05:01,828
Not to mention, you'd also have to sleep

62
00:05:01,828 --> 00:05:04,668
in the same room with them for four consecutive nights.

63
00:05:04,908 --> 00:05:06,048
Okay, I get it.

64
00:05:06,388 --> 00:05:07,728
You don't have to be so blunt.

65
00:05:08,008 --> 00:05:09,368
You could be more tactful.

66
00:05:09,368 --> 00:05:10,688
This is really awkward.

67
00:05:11,888 --> 00:05:14,348
Well, I know pro shogi players like you

68
00:05:14,348 --> 00:05:15,888
don't often have a lot of free time.

69
00:05:17,048 --> 00:05:17,728
It's true.

70
00:05:18,328 --> 00:05:20,068
I do have quite a few matches a month.

71
00:05:20,988 --> 00:05:23,408
Shogi is kind of like baseball or boxing in that way.

72
00:05:24,068 --> 00:05:25,348
There's not a lot of time off.

73
00:05:26,108 --> 00:05:28,068
So, what does a pro athlete do

74
00:05:28,068 --> 00:05:29,488
when he or she has some free time?

75
00:05:32,288 --> 00:05:32,728
Exactly.

76
00:05:33,248 --> 00:05:33,928
They train.

77
00:05:34,788 --> 00:05:36,608
Shogi players are like pro athletes.

78
00:05:36,608 --> 00:05:38,668
On days without matches,

79
00:05:39,108 --> 00:05:41,068
we spend our time practicing or studying.

80
00:05:41,568 --> 00:05:42,648
We set up and examine

81
00:05:42,648 --> 00:05:44,328
countless game records left behind

82
00:05:44,328 --> 00:05:45,148
by our predecessors

83
00:05:45,148 --> 00:05:46,668
and hold study sessions

84
00:05:46,668 --> 00:05:48,028
with other shogi players

85
00:05:48,028 --> 00:05:49,668
practicing against each other,

86
00:05:50,188 --> 00:05:52,448
investigating new tactics and strategies.

87
00:05:53,708 --> 00:05:55,628
But, if you don't participate

88
00:05:55,628 --> 00:05:56,928
in any school activities,

89
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:58,928
what's the point of re-enrolling in high school?

90
00:05:58,928 --> 00:06:01,128
I don't really know.

91
00:06:01,428 --> 00:06:01,828
Huh?

92
00:06:02,228 --> 00:06:02,748
Hey!

93
00:06:03,088 --> 00:06:04,588
Don't just agree with me.

94
00:06:11,588 --> 00:06:13,208
You don't have a home.

95
00:06:13,788 --> 00:06:14,848
You don't have a family.

96
00:06:15,408 --> 00:06:16,948
And you don't go to school.

97
00:06:17,968 --> 00:06:19,648
You don't have any friends, either.

98
00:06:20,488 --> 00:06:21,748
You don't belong anywhere.

99
00:06:21,748 --> 00:06:24,408
There's no place for you, is there?

100
00:06:30,388 --> 00:06:31,828
That's what Kyoko said.

101
00:06:32,588 --> 00:06:34,648
She nailed me right in the center of my heart.

102
00:06:35,608 --> 00:06:37,788
But it didn't make me angry or sad.

103
00:06:37,788 --> 00:06:41,868
I just thought

104
00:06:41,868 --> 00:06:44,368
you couldn't be more, right?

105
00:06:48,628 --> 00:06:50,088
That's exactly why

106
00:06:50,088 --> 00:06:51,508
I wanted to become a pro.

107
00:06:55,828 --> 00:06:57,788
I thought if I could support myself

108
00:06:57,788 --> 00:06:58,748
with shogi alone,

109
00:06:59,248 --> 00:07:01,368
it would eventually become

110
00:07:01,368 --> 00:07:02,948
the place where I belong.

111
00:07:03,988 --> 00:07:05,888
So I began desperately clinging

112
00:07:05,888 --> 00:07:06,888
to the shogi board.

113
00:07:07,788 --> 00:07:10,388
And then,

114
00:07:10,808 --> 00:07:11,988
my dream came true.

115
00:07:12,608 --> 00:07:13,708
It became a reality.

116
00:07:28,748 --> 00:07:30,728
I hardly had anything to unpack,

117
00:07:31,228 --> 00:07:32,848
so it didn't take me long to move in.

118
00:07:37,788 --> 00:07:53,188
For some time after that,

119
00:07:53,548 --> 00:07:54,808
I lived in an empty room

120
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:57,188
without any curtains or a TV.

121
00:07:57,568 --> 00:07:58,508
I felt drained

122
00:07:58,508 --> 00:08:00,108
like an empty battery.

123
00:08:00,108 --> 00:08:02,928
All I really did was focus on shogi

124
00:08:02,928 --> 00:08:04,488
and go to school sometimes.

125
00:08:05,108 --> 00:08:05,748
Other than that,

126
00:08:06,288 --> 00:08:07,808
I spent a lot of time sleeping.

127
00:08:09,608 --> 00:08:10,668
For some reason,

128
00:08:11,428 --> 00:08:13,308
I felt even more tired every day.

129
00:08:15,908 --> 00:08:17,628
At the house I used to live in,

130
00:08:18,008 --> 00:08:19,288
I helped out with the chores,

131
00:08:19,808 --> 00:08:21,428
so I pretty much kept that up.

132
00:08:21,428 --> 00:08:23,968
But when it came to making food,

133
00:08:23,968 --> 00:08:26,088
I couldn't even force myself

134
00:08:26,088 --> 00:08:26,868
to cook rice.

135
00:08:27,988 --> 00:08:29,468
So I stopped trying.

136
00:08:33,388 --> 00:08:35,048
The first year was fine.

137
00:08:35,048 --> 00:08:38,048
I was able to get by

138
00:08:38,048 --> 00:08:38,828
using the savings

139
00:08:38,828 --> 00:08:39,948
I'd built up until then.

140
00:08:43,568 --> 00:08:44,868
There are 30 people

141
00:08:44,868 --> 00:08:45,848
in Class C1.

142
00:08:46,608 --> 00:08:47,828
Each person faces off

143
00:08:47,828 --> 00:08:48,748
against 10 opponents.

144
00:08:49,388 --> 00:08:50,048
The two people

145
00:08:50,048 --> 00:08:50,848
with the most wins

146
00:08:50,848 --> 00:08:51,428
in the class

147
00:08:51,428 --> 00:08:52,348
get to move on

148
00:08:52,348 --> 00:08:53,148
to the next level,

149
00:08:53,608 --> 00:08:54,388
Class B2.

150
00:08:54,388 --> 00:08:56,228
You have to win

151
00:08:56,228 --> 00:08:57,848
at least 9 out of 10 matches

152
00:08:57,848 --> 00:08:58,868
for a chance

153
00:08:58,868 --> 00:08:59,568
at being promoted

154
00:08:59,568 --> 00:09:00,588
to the next class.

155
00:09:03,248 --> 00:09:04,228
But this year

156
00:09:04,228 --> 00:09:05,368
hasn't been going well.

157
00:09:07,608 --> 00:09:08,908
I lost two matches

158
00:09:08,908 --> 00:09:09,368
in a row

159
00:09:09,368 --> 00:09:10,268
for the first time.

160
00:09:14,868 --> 00:09:16,208
I was caught off guard

161
00:09:16,208 --> 00:09:17,068
by my defeats

162
00:09:17,068 --> 00:09:20,648
and lost my chance

163
00:09:20,648 --> 00:09:21,268
at advancement.

164
00:09:24,388 --> 00:09:25,768
All right.

165
00:09:26,128 --> 00:09:37,648
Let's go.

166
00:09:51,908 --> 00:09:52,868
Let's go.

167
00:09:52,868 --> 00:10:11,808
I swam, and swam, and swam, and swam, and swam,

168
00:10:13,348 --> 00:10:18,548
and swam, and swam, and swam,

169
00:10:18,548 --> 00:10:23,128
and swam to the very end

170
00:10:23,128 --> 00:10:27,208
until I finally made it to the island.

171
00:10:33,048 --> 00:10:35,548
I thought I would be okay after getting there.

172
00:10:38,988 --> 00:10:40,828
If only I could get there.

173
00:10:42,668 --> 00:10:44,808
If I could just stay there on that island.

174
00:10:46,588 --> 00:10:48,388
And if I hadn't gotten greedy.

175
00:10:48,968 --> 00:10:50,368
Making too many wishes.

176
00:10:52,668 --> 00:10:55,028
As long as I accepted stagnation.

177
00:10:55,448 --> 00:10:58,048
And as long as I stopped myself from thinking.

178
00:10:59,888 --> 00:11:01,628
Then I would have reached my goal.

179
00:11:05,488 --> 00:11:06,368
If so.

180
00:11:07,068 --> 00:11:09,788
I wouldn't have to plunge back into that stormy sea.

181
00:11:10,488 --> 00:11:12,108
I wouldn't have a reason to go back.

182
00:11:12,808 --> 00:11:14,208
Or to move forward.

183
00:11:14,948 --> 00:11:16,908
I'd never have to swim like that again.

184
00:11:18,548 --> 00:11:19,768
Weapon Minister who were waiting for us.

185
00:11:19,768 --> 00:11:21,768
No way.

186
00:11:22,188 --> 00:11:23,388
We'll get people harder.

187
00:11:24,028 --> 00:11:24,368
I'm sorry.

188
00:11:25,368 --> 00:11:27,348
We'll be right back.

189
00:11:27,428 --> 00:11:27,888
We'll be right back.

190
00:11:27,968 --> 00:11:28,468
We'll be right back.

191
00:11:28,568 --> 00:11:29,448
OK?

192
00:11:29,568 --> 00:11:29,648
Then we will have to go forward.

193
00:11:29,888 --> 00:11:30,268
I will be right back.

194
00:11:30,528 --> 00:11:31,068
We'll be.

195
00:11:31,128 --> 00:11:31,588
Then we will be right back.

196
00:11:31,648 --> 00:11:31,988
We'll be right back.

197
00:11:32,028 --> 00:11:32,488
Go ahead.

198
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:33,108
Baby, come on.

199
00:11:33,168 --> 00:11:33,588
Go ahead!

200
00:11:33,648 --> 00:11:34,108
Hey!

201
00:11:34,128 --> 00:11:34,328
Come on!

202
00:11:34,408 --> 00:11:35,068
Come on!

203
00:11:35,288 --> 00:11:35,308
Baby, come on!

204
00:11:35,448 --> 00:11:35,748
Now we're up!

205
00:11:35,928 --> 00:11:36,548
Come on!

206
00:11:36,548 --> 00:11:36,768
�잖 saga-

207
00:11:36,768 --> 00:12:06,748
The first time I saw him I thought

208
00:12:06,748 --> 00:12:13,748
Wow what a cold guy

209
00:12:13,748 --> 00:12:31,748
But I can't remember when that first time was at all

210
00:12:31,748 --> 00:12:40,748
For as long as I can remember, he just always seemed to be there

211
00:12:40,748 --> 00:12:47,748
Toji Soya

212
00:12:47,748 --> 00:12:56,748
In our small universe, he was the child of God

213
00:12:56,748 --> 00:13:06,748
Where's your big rice soccer ball? No special lunch today, huh?

214
00:13:06,748 --> 00:13:08,748
No, sir

215
00:13:08,748 --> 00:13:13,748
Too cold to sit outside, huh? But it's not much warmer in here either

216
00:13:13,748 --> 00:13:18,748
Have you seen this? It just came out

217
00:13:18,748 --> 00:13:21,748
It's the latest modern shogi

218
00:13:21,748 --> 00:13:25,748
I finally made it! My challenge got published

219
00:13:25,748 --> 00:13:28,748
No way! Oh wow, that's awesome

220
00:13:28,748 --> 00:13:30,748
That's awesome, nice

221
00:13:30,748 --> 00:13:32,748
It's a pretty good setup you've got here

222
00:13:32,748 --> 00:13:35,748
3-1 bishop, 2-3 king, 1-3 gold, same knight

223
00:13:35,748 --> 00:13:38,748
3-3 dragon horse, 1-4 king, 1-3 dragon horse, same king

224
00:13:38,748 --> 00:13:41,748
2-3 gold, 1-4 king, 2-6 knight, same gold

225
00:13:41,748 --> 00:13:43,748
2-4 knight, checkmate and 13 moves, right?

226
00:13:43,748 --> 00:13:45,748
Yeah, he did!

227
00:13:45,748 --> 00:13:46,748
That was fast!

228
00:13:46,748 --> 00:13:47,748
It took me a week to make!

229
00:13:47,748 --> 00:13:48,748
You made it look simple

230
00:13:48,748 --> 00:13:50,748
But I guess it all makes sense

231
00:13:50,748 --> 00:13:52,748
You're a pro after all

232
00:13:55,748 --> 00:13:57,748
Grandmaster Toji Soya

233
00:13:57,748 --> 00:13:59,748
He's having another great season

234
00:13:59,748 --> 00:14:04,748
He's already been successful in defending his Kishin, Seiryu and Gyoku show titles this year

235
00:14:04,748 --> 00:14:05,748
So, what's he like?

236
00:14:05,748 --> 00:14:07,748
I honestly wouldn't know

237
00:14:07,748 --> 00:14:10,748
You've never met him? But you're both pros

238
00:14:13,748 --> 00:14:16,748
We've never actually talked before

239
00:14:16,748 --> 00:14:18,748
But I've seen him around

240
00:14:20,748 --> 00:14:22,748
We're both in different classes

241
00:14:22,748 --> 00:14:25,748
Grandmaster Soya currently holds most of the titles

242
00:14:25,748 --> 00:14:29,748
So, I rarely see him at tournaments anymore

243
00:14:30,748 --> 00:14:32,748
I can't believe he's as old as I am

244
00:14:32,748 --> 00:14:34,748
How weird

245
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:36,748
Wow, he hasn't aged a bit

246
00:14:36,748 --> 00:14:39,748
He looks the same as he did when he was a teenager

247
00:14:39,748 --> 00:14:42,748
It's like time just came to a complete stop for him

248
00:14:42,748 --> 00:14:43,748
Strange

249
00:14:43,748 --> 00:14:46,748
The first time I saw him, I was in middle school

250
00:14:46,748 --> 00:14:48,748
He was featured in an article titled

251
00:14:48,748 --> 00:14:49,748
A middle school pro is born

252
00:14:49,748 --> 00:14:50,748
Huh?

253
00:14:50,748 --> 00:14:51,748
That's right

254
00:14:51,748 --> 00:14:53,748
Come to think of it, the first time I saw you

255
00:14:53,748 --> 00:14:56,748
Was in the same kind of article in this magazine

256
00:14:57,748 --> 00:14:59,748
Oh, that's right

257
00:14:59,748 --> 00:15:01,748
When we're just sitting here talking as usual

258
00:15:01,748 --> 00:15:04,748
I forget, you're actually a pretty amazing guy

259
00:15:04,748 --> 00:15:07,748
Even though you usually end up having lunch all by yourself

260
00:15:07,748 --> 00:15:11,748
And I never really know for sure whether you're actually here or not

261
00:15:11,748 --> 00:15:15,748
Excuse me, but can you please try to be a little more tactful?

262
00:15:16,748 --> 00:15:23,748
In the entire history of Shogi, there were only four players that ever became pros while they were still in middle school

263
00:15:24,748 --> 00:15:29,748
Those four players went on to win even more titles and eventually earned the name Grandmaster

264
00:15:29,748 --> 00:15:32,748
But as for me, the fifth player

265
00:15:35,748 --> 00:15:36,748
We expect great things

266
00:15:36,748 --> 00:15:39,748
They're already calling you the future Grandmaster

267
00:15:39,748 --> 00:15:42,748
Don't worry, sometimes even prodigies have slumps

268
00:15:44,748 --> 00:15:46,748
Hey, I thought you were supposed to be good

269
00:15:46,748 --> 00:15:47,748
Better get it together

270
00:15:47,748 --> 00:15:50,748
